  "history_summaries": [
    "Round 1/3: Fix width truncation in leftCount/rightCount/emptyCount/invalidCount computations. Root cause: .reduce(_+_) on 1-bit asUInt values produces a 1-bit wire, truncating counts of up to 7. Changed from .map(_.asUInt).reduce(_+_) to PopCount(...) which correctly infers log2(8)=3 bits. This fixes the constant-false optimization that caused exactly_three_left_cars and exactly_three_right_cars to fail at every cycle. Also fixes homologous assertions (exactly_one_empty_slot, no_invalid_slot_values) and prevents width issues in assertStableWhen calls (valid_move_preserves_left/right_count). Target assertion label 'exactly_three_left_cars' preserved exactly.",
    "Round 2/3: Fix two remaining assertion bugs. (1) no_move_no_empty_change: added prevValid=RegNext(valid) and changed condition to !valid && !prevValid to skip checking on the transition cycle where a valid move legitimately changed empty. (2) valid_move_relocates_empty_correctly: changed property to empty === RegNext(io.move) to capture io.move at the time of the valid move and compare against it in the next cycle, avoiding false failure when io.move changes. Both assertions preserved with exact original labels. No homologous assertions found for either fix after source inspection."
